it's time to supercharge your summer  movie season  i'm britt morin founder and ceo of  britain co and i've teamed up with dq to  welcome you to fandango's family movie  night  today we're going to be making the  cutest little capes for the little  heroes in your family  using stuff you probably already have at  home  it's time to watch those superhero  movies in style  alright let's get started by collecting  everything you'll need for this project  first in order to fit your child you'll  need roughly an 18 by 24 piece of  felt and some accessorizing felt colors  so you can make your fun shapes and  patterns  then you'll need fabric scissors fabric  glue or a glue gun  a pen for tracing and a couple pieces of  velcro to make it stick  all right first step is to cut the shape  of your cape you're going to take  your biggest piece of fabric and cut out  a large  trapezoid so i've already cut one side  here  and i'm going to measure this other side  just by my eyes  and make a diagonal line all the way  to the end next you're going to make a  u-shape along the back so that you have  little tabs that can act like the neck  straps  all right next you're going to cut out  different types of shapes from your  colored felt you can make stars  lightning bolts  even an earth and then decide which one  you want to glue onto your cape  i'm gonna go with this lightning bolt  just use your fabric glue  to spread out along the felt  and place it wherever you want  as a final step you're going to take  your two velcro tabs  and put one underneath  your first tab here on the felt  and the other is going to go on top  of your second it fits perfectly right  now your little one can take on the  world  treat your kiddo and yourself to an oreo  fudge brownie blizzard from dq  next time you're out and about thanks  for watching and be sure to check out  fandango now for more superhero films  for the whole family
 

